Taylor is a 23-year-old recent graduate from China, working part-time while saving for further studies, and sharing the house to cut costs. An ISFJ, Taylor is extremely conscientious and value-driven, though they can be surprisingly aggressive in their opinions. They are a natural leader, always taking charge in house meetings, yet they struggle with trust and often prefer to do things themselves. Taylor is deeply committed to the community, volunteering at local shelters, and enjoys helping others, but their low agreeableness means they can be blunt and judgmental. They are a creature of habit, valuing routine and stability, and they maintain a meticulous schedule for their jobs and studies. Despite their high conscientiousness, Taylor has a chaotic living space, with clothes on the floor and a desk covered in papers. They are also risk-tolerant when it comes to health and safety, often eating expired food and ignoring minor injuries. In the household, Taylor handles the maintenance and coordinating with the landlord, using their excellent organizational skills. They are tech-savvy in a reluctant way, preferring traditional methods, and they spend only two to four hours daily on screens. Taylor's frustration stems from financial pressure and caregiving duties for an elder relative, which often leaves them stressed and sleep-deprived. However, they are resilient and rarely show vulnerability, masking their worries with a determined smile. Their competitiveness pushes them to excel academically and professionally, but it can also create tension with their more laid-back housemates. Despite their faults, Taylor's dedication and reliability make them a pillar of the share house, even if they often forget to participate in fun activities.

